sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: swamp/workflows/workflow-operation-task-vm-image-build.yaml, docs/reference/compute-drivers.md#build-the-base-image and #the-topology-seed, docs/cli/README.md design rules R2-R4.
  %% Kept: rule 14 and 16 do not apply: `orbit-agent command` exits 0 and prints `{ok:false}` on a refusal (apps/agent/src/command/mod.rs), so each agent call keeps a typed reply check; `image.start-phase` returns no main PID (Observation in apps/agent/src/commands/image_recipe/lifecycle.rs), so the PID is one `systemctl show` read.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 15 (no `plan` step), 6 (boot, prepare, smoke merges), 8 (owner check before the phases), 18 (reset and cleanup as one forEach; Pi staging beside boot), 19 (cleanup on completed), 22 (each Node action one `@swamp/ssh exec` argv).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · recipe image build for an Incus host
  %% kind: task_vm.image_build
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Incus host<br/>Node 13 over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit build 61<br/>host Node 13 · task #5182
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `php artisan task-vms:build-recipe` (also `--retry`, `--rebuild`), `task-vms:build-image 13`, or the per-minute recipe reconcile
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - Node 13 is an active task VM host in `settings.task_vms`, and its recipe is the desired one
  %%> - the agent pin matches the Gateway delivery, else the build refuses before any step
  %%> Result:
  %%> - build 61 recorded as running; the full intent holds the recipe document, identity, project, pool, builder and smoke names, SSH target with host keys, and every agent envelope
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-image-build
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `operation_id`, `node_id` 13, `kind`, and the full public `intent`; there is no secret, so `execution_secrets` is empty
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the Gateway computes each agent envelope `{agent_sha256, deadline_ms, input}` at admission, so no `plan` step re-reads the intent (rule 15)
  %%> Budget:
  %%> - 2,400 seconds; `queueTimeout` 30 seconds
  SW->>H: Install the pinned agent<br/>install-agent · restart-agent
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `@swamp/cfgmgmt/fetch` downloads the release's agent build from `intent.agent_url` to `/usr/local/bin/orbit-agent`, root-owned, mode 0755, and checks `sha256:<agent_sha256>`
  %%> - one `@swamp/ssh exec` argv `systemctl try-restart orbit-agent.service` restarts the observer when it runs
  %%> Why:
  %%> - every later agent call carries the release pin; without this step a pin move fails each call with `agent.version_mismatch`
  SW->>H: Remove earlier attempts<br/>reset · forEach builder, smoke
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `forEach` over `tvm-image-61` and `tvm-image-61-smoke`; each item runs `sudo -n -- orbit-agent command incus.vm` with `remove_instance`
  %%> - an absent VM counts as removed, so a fresh build passes at once
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a resumed or retried attempt may find its own VMs from before
  SW->>H: Launch the builder<br/>launch · incus.vm create_image
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `incus.vm` `create_image` from the stock source image, with the account key, resource limits and builder account mode
  %%> - the agent renders cloud-init, attaches the configuration disk and removes the NoCloud seed templates before the first start
  SW->>H: Boot the builder<br/>boot · incus wait · agent.install
  %%> How:
  %%> - `incus wait tvm-image-61 agent --timeout 600`, then `cloud-init status --wait` in the guest
  %%> - `incus file push --mode 0700` of the host's pinned agent; the guest's `agent.install` checks it against the pin
  %%> - `guest.cloud-init` reports readiness, `image.inspect-phase` records the boot id, `image.owner` checks UID and GID 1000
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the owner check moves here from after the phases, so a taken UID fails before any package installs (rule 8)
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - a failed agent wait is `task_vm.bootstrap_timeout`, another boot step `task_vm.bootstrap_failed`
  opt recipe pins a Pi build
    SW->>H: Stage the Pi build<br/>pi-fetch · pi-check · pi-push
    %%> How:
    %%> - `@swamp/ssh copy` of the pinned binary from the Gateway Node to 209, `sha256sum -c` against its pin, copy to Node 13, then `incus file push --mode 0600` to `/var/cache/orbit/pi/<sha256>.bin`
    %%> - fetch and check run beside the builder boot; only the push waits for it (rule 18)
    %%> When:
    %%> - skipped by `guard` when the recipe has no Pi build
  end
  loop each recipe phase
    SW->>H: Run the phase<br/><phase>-start · wait · inspect
    %%> Phases:
    %%> - `apt-source`, `packages`, `javascript`, `rust`, `agent`, `pi`, in this order
    %%> How:
    %%> - `image.start-phase` starts or observes the guest's bounded systemd service; one `systemctl show --property=MainPID` read gives its main PID
    %%> - `timeout 1500 tail --pid=PID -f /dev/null` waits; a `guard` skips it when the phase already ended
    %%> - `image.inspect-phase` must report `complete` for the same boot id
    %%> Reply checks:
    %%> - the agent exits 0 and prints `{ok:false}` on a refusal, so a typed reply step on 209 fails with the agent's own error code
  end
  SW->>H: Prepare and clean<br/>prepare · ssh-enable · clean
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `image.recipe-marker`, `image.boot`, `systemctl enable ssh.service`, the Orbit root CA in the trust store, then `image.clean`
  %%> - `slot-identity-unit` pushes `orbit-slot-identity.service` with `incus file push`, and `slot-identity-enable` enables it; the unit is idle without an identity volume
  %%> - the `slot-units-*` steps push the slot target, the observer unit and its drop-in, the Pi unit and the WireGuard drop-in, and `slot-units-enable` enables the target; each unit starts only when its identity file exists
  %%> - `image.clean` removes machine, SSH, Incus and service identities and refuses an enrolled guest
  %%> Why:
  %%> - one action that readies the guest for publication; the separate metadata and marker steps merge (rule 6)
  SW->>H: Publish the candidate<br/>publish · incus.image publish
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `incus.image` stops and publishes the builder, then promotes the immutable candidate alias
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the published fingerprint; 209 decodes it in TypeScript into the seed and promote envelopes
  SW->>H: Smoke the candidate<br/>smoke · image.check · ssh-smoke
  %%> How:
  %%> - removes the builder, launches `tvm-image-61-smoke` from the candidate, boots it as in step 4
  %%> - `image.verify` checks the recipe software, `image.check` the account, key and lean boot, and `systemctl is-active ssh.service`
  %%> - `smoke-slot-identity` runs `systemctl is-enabled orbit-slot-identity.service`; the smoke VM has no identity volume, so the unit stays skipped
  %%> - `smoke-slot-units` checks that `orbit-slot.target` is enabled and that the target, the observer, Pi and WireGuard are all inactive
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a failed smoke check stops the build before promotion
  SW->>H: Build the topology seed<br/>seed · finish-seed
  %%> How:
  %%> - `incus.build-topology-seed` builds `orbit-topology-seed-<12 hex>-new` inside the smoke VM
  %%> - deletes the smoke VM, then `incus.volume` renames the seed to its final name
  %%> When:
  %%> - a finished seed already present builds nothing
  SW->>H: Promote and prune<br/>promote · prune · complete
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `incus.image` moves the host's base alias to the candidate, then prunes old recipe images and their seeds
  %%> End check:
  %%> - the native `assert` step `complete` checks the 64-hex fingerprint and the prune reply; this is the one end check (rule 9)
  SW->>H: Remove builder and smoke<br/>cleanup · completed · forEach
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `forEach` runs `incus.vm` `remove_instance` for the builder and the smoke VM, then removes the staged Pi copies on 209 and Node 13
  %%> When:
  %%> - always, with the condition `completed`: after success, failure or a cancel request (rule 19)
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - `task_vm.image_cleanup_failed`
  alt image promoted
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>fingerprint · phase times
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - step statuses, the published fingerprint, and each phase's start and end
    Note over GW: Record build 61<br/>succeeded · base alias moved
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the build row stores the image location; new task VMs on Node 13 claim it
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a refused agent reply keeps its own code; other steps map to `task_vm.image_build_failed`
    Note over GW: Mark build 61 failed<br/>previous image stays
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the promoted image stays in service; `task-vms:build-recipe --retry` starts a fresh stock attempt
  end
